# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: install-libraries-omits-runtime-data-files -- the installed ASDF systems lack the data files their sources read (getcname tables, cadtui locales, the drawing template)
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-install-libraries-omits-runtime-data-files
#+DATE: 2026-11-19

* Symptom

=make install-libraries= (=install-lisp-systems=, and the release-libraries
artefact that mirrors it) copies only =*.lisp= and =*.asd= under
=<PREFIX>/share/common-lisp/source/clautolisp/=. On poseidon, the 2.4.16
and the 2.4.33 installs both have =cador/= and =drawing/= holding only
=source/= and =tests/=, and =cadtui/= likewise. A program that does
=(asdf:load-system "clautolisp")= from the installed tree, which is what
the install is for (dwg-identifier, for one), then gets an engine that is
quietly wrong:

- =cador/source/getcname.lisp= embeds =../data/getcname/*.sexp= at compile
  time. With no file present it embeds NIL, so =GETCNAME= returns NIL even
  for "_LINE" -> "LINE" and loses every localised name (ÉTIRER under fr_FR).
  Nothing signals.
- =cadtui/source/locale.lisp= embeds =../data/locale/*/*.sexp= the same
  way. cadtui therefore has no fr_FR / de_DE / es_ES keywords or verbs.
- =drawing-template-path= is =drawing/template/empty-drawing.dxf= relative
  to =clautolisp/drawing=. NEW / startup documents fail with "no bundled
  template".

These are exactly the 41 cador failures of
=issues/closed/make-test-loads-installed-clautolisp.issue=, where the suite
ran against the installed tree by mistake.

* Cause

The comment above =LISP_SOURCE_FILES= in =clautolisp/Makefile= says:
"Every component of every system is a plain `:file' (i.e. .lisp), so
.lisp + .asd is the complete set." That is true of ASDF components. It is
not true of the files the sources read through =*compile-file-truename*= /
=*load-truename*= or =asdf:system-relative-pathname=, which no .asd
declares.

* Files concerned (survey at 2.4.34)

- =cador/data/getcname/*.sexp= (compile time)
- =cadtui/data/locale/<locale>/*.sexp= (compile time, and reloaded at
  load time from =system-relative-pathname=)
- =drawing/template/empty-drawing.dxf= (run time)
- probably not: =examples/*/*.dcl=, =autolisp-file-compat/scenarios/*.sexp=
  (examples and test scenarios, not engine data). Decide when fixing.

* Fix directions

1. Install the data trees with the sources: extend =LISP_SOURCE_FILES= (or
   add a =LISP_DATA_FILES= list) to =*/data/**= and =drawing/template/*=,
   and keep the release-libraries artefact in step (root Makefile).
2. Make them visible to ASDF too, as =:static-file= components of the
   systems that read them. =getcname.lisp= and =locale.lisp= would then
   also be recompiled when a table changes, which today needs a touch or a
   full rebuild.
3. Fail loudly: =%embed-getcname-tables= and =%embed-locale-tree= should
   signal at compile time when their glob matches nothing, rather than bake
   an empty table.
4. Regression test: =install-lisp-systems= into a scratch =DESTDIR=, load
   =clautolisp= from there in a fresh image (registry limited to that
   tree), and check getcname "_LINE" and =drawing-template-path=.

* Resolved

2026-11-19, clautolisp 2.4.35 / alfe 2.4.35, branch
=fix-install-libraries-omits-runtime-data-files= (stacked on
=fix-make-test-loads-installed-clautolisp=, which took 2.4.34).

- Direction 1: =install-lisp-systems= now also installs =LISP_DATA_FILES=,
  every file under a =<subsystem>/data/= or =<subsystem>/template/=
  directory outside =tests/=, =third-party/=, =build/= and =.cache/=.
  Today that is the 11 files listed above. The release-libraries
  artefact follows automatically: =stage-libraries= runs this same
  target. The examples' =.dcl= and the file-compat scenarios stay out;
  they are not engine data.
- Direction 3: =%embed-getcname-tables= and =%embed-locale-tree= signal an
  error at compile time when their glob matches nothing. An install
  without its data now fails to compile with a message naming the
  missing directory, instead of loading with empty tables.
- Direction 4: =make -C clautolisp test-installed-libraries=, run by
  =make test= and by =test:clautolisp:sbcl= in both CIs, takes about 13 s.
  It runs =install-lisp-systems= into a scratch =DESTDIR= and loads
  =clautolisp/drawing=, =clautolisp/cador= and =clautolisp/cadtui= from
  that tree ALONE (=:ignore-inherited-configuration=; Quicklisp still
  supplies the third-party systems). It then checks getcname
  ="_LINE"= => "LINE", BricsCAD V26 fr_FR ="_STRETCH"= => "ÉTIRER",
  cadtui's fr_FR locale, and the installed drawing template. Before the
  fix it gave 4 failures. With the data tree deleted from the scratch
  install it now stops on the new compile error.
- Direction 2 (=:static-file= components, so editing a table recompiles
  its reader) is not done. ASDF has no globs, so every data file would
  have to be listed in the .asd. cadtui's load-time reload already
  covers a source-tree build. Left for when a table changes often
  enough to matter.

